 36MG    C(37MG,36MGG):XUNDL-4         2014KO14                           201412
 36MG c  Includes Pb({+37}Mg,{+36}Mg|g)                                         
 36MG c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2014Ko14:                          
 36MG c  Phys Rev Lett 112, 242501 (2014)                                       
 36MG c  Compiled by J. C. Batchelder (ORNL/ORAU), December 10, 2014            
 36MG c  Coulomb and nuclear dominated 1 neutron removal reaction:              
 36MG c  Projectile: {+37}Mg secondary beam produced by projectile              
 36MG2c  fragmentation at RIKEN with E({+37}Mg)=240 MeV/u mid target            
 36MG3c  energy for C target (thickness 2.54 g/cm{+2}) and ({+37}Mg)=244 MeV/u  
 36MG4c  mid target energy for Pb target (thickness 3.37 g/cm{+2}) with typical 
 36MG5c  intensity of 6 pps                                                     
 36MG c  Detectors: {+36}Mg residues produced were identified by their          
 36MG2c  B|r, tof, and |DE using the Zero Degree Spectrometer and the           
 36MG3c  |g-rays detected with the DALI2 detector array at RIBF-RIKEN facility. 
 36MG c  Measured: E|g, I|g, ({+36}Mg residue)|g-coin and cross-section based   
 36MG2c  on known 2+ |) 0+ and 4+ |) 2+ |g-rays in {+36}Mg.                     
 36MG c  Measured the total |s=80 mb {I4} for C({+37}Mg,{+36}Mg) reaction.      
 36MG2c  Measured partial |s for population of excited 2{++}{-1} and 0{++}{-1}  
 36MG3c  states as 42 mb {I7} and 38 mb {I8}, respectively                      
